raka is still highly effective taking down humans, Claimed/Ridden, fellow werewolves, and others using the same tactics as the Hosts. A tanky Blood Talon is still effective in battle against any prey. The manipulate-human-world abitlies of the Iron Masters might be ideal for hunting humans, but it is still effective when dealing with any prey. And so on.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about affinity Gifts. They're a bit misleading, because you really have to look at the cross section of Gifts by Renown. A low Purity werewolf isn't going to be using a lot of Purity-based abilities, even if he does have affinity for purchasing them. A high Puritiy wolf, meanwhile, is going to be attracted to picking up some non-affinity Gifts that work well with his Renown score. Because of that, you want to look at the Tribal-affinity merits and Rites as well as the affinity Gifts; the former two are exclusive to the Tribe, while the latter two are not.<br /> <br /> As for that &quot;I'm a role player and don't care about mechanics&quot; bit? Onyx Path writers are very good at using mechanics to support the themes of the associated tribe/auspice. All the mechanics support the goals of the splats, and the splats defined what the mechanics should be like. The two are tightly interconnected. If you want to know how a Storm Lord hunts, you look at their affinities - merits, rites, renown-based affinity gifts together. Choosing a Tribe is choosing the tools you want to hunt with. Don't want to be accused of being a min-maxer, that's fine. I'm not advocating optimization or anything like that. However, its unavoidable that mechanics inform the story and roleplaying aspects of the characters, and choosing the right abilities that complement your concept does make the game more fun. If you go Storm Lord, and are stuck with a suite of powers that involve inspiriing allies and maneuvering when you wanted neither is a bit of an issue.<br /> <br /> Plus, you're the one who was contemplating a Tribe just so you could start with Purity 3, and now you're looking at Iron Masters just for Technolgy (which could easily get at a 2exp penalty for all of the facets). Nevermind that Warding would be just as awesome for keeping tabs on your territory for another superhero-ish ability. Or that the Hunters in Darkness have exclusive powers to practically teleport across their cityscape. Or that Irraka/Hunter In Darkness vibes with the whole loner bit.<br /> <br /> You wanted an opinon, I gave an informed opinion based on an analysis of the 2e material. Cheers, I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to offend you. I'm sorry if I did. I wasn't trying to imply anything. Your original post just gave me a sense of &quot;Here's what would be advantageous to do&quot; and I thought I may have miscommunicated my request. Mea culpa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:50:55-08:00","id":771597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771323-not-sure-what-the-best-tribe-would-be-for-this-character-i-m-making?p=771569#post771569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b>wasn't</b> trying to offend you. I'm sorry if I did. I wasn't trying to imply anything. Your original post just gave me a sense of &quot;Here's what would be advantageous to do&quot; and I thought I may have miscommunicated my request. Mea culpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed for your convenience <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We don't want more misunderstandings, now do we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:15:41-08:00","id":771614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771323-not-sure-what-the-best-tribe-would-be-for-this-character-i-m-making?p=771597#post771597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fixed for your convenience <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We don't want more misunderstandings, now do we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Mea maxima culpa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:21:27-08:00","id":771618,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'd like to correct myself in claiming that the Technology gift was Iron Master only. Of course you can get it out of tribe for an increased cost, though I'd still say he sounds like Iron Master all the way.<br /> <br /> While I disagree with pretty much everything MCN has said, it's definitely not wrong to consider renown and synergy with tribal merits and and benefits. I think Iron Masters work best, but I the concept works with HiD and even the other tribes to a lesser extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":".  I dunno Ephsy, I just don't know. 11-22-2015, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:23:45-08:00","id":771619,"title":"","content":"On topic: Go Iron Master.<br /> <br /> Off-topic: Why is people addressing the Hunters in Darkness as HtD instead of HiD?<br /> <br /> Color me disagreeing with MCN entirely as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-22-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:29:42-08:00","id":771621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771323-not-sure-what-the-best-tribe-would-be-for-this-character-i-m-making?p=771619#post771619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic: Go Iron Master.<br /> <br /> Off-topic: Why is people addressing the Hunters in Darkness as HtD instead of HiD?<br /> <br /> Color me disagreeing with MCN entirely as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because they're mixing HiD w/ WtF<br /> <br /> And in my case because I haven't slept in a fortnight.<br /> <br /> I should really be sleeping instead of designing a werewolf running around baltimore in his pajamas.<br /> <br /> But that isn't how we made this country great.<br /> <br /> No sir.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what is the disagreement exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:05:31-08:00","id":771745,"title":"","content":"That you should take BT for Rahu; Ithaeur for BS; Irraka for HiD; Cahalith for SL; or Elodoth for IM, on the context of some hyper specialization.<br /> <br /> My Meninna Ithaeur would fuck the Host shit up with an entire umia pressed to the task. Flood plague tunnels, burn Gauntlet webs and the spiders within to a crisp as well. <br /> <br /> My Cahalith Farsil Luhal would sick every law enforcement agency on the neighboring Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:26:32-08:00","id":771762,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ephsy here, you should not feel at all obligated to choose a certain tribe for your Auspice.<br /> <br /> The writers certaintly did not have such intent. While it is true that each Auspice seems to have a tribe that fits it better (and vice versa), do not forget that they spent quite a lot of word count explaining how the members of each tribe use their Auspice's strengths in the hunt of their chosen prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:26:53-08:00","id":771764,"title":"","content":"Tribe is what a werewolf does. Auspice is how they do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T17:43:21-08:00","id":771931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771323-not-sure-what-the-best-tribe-would-be-for-this-character-i-m-making?p=771460#post771460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with Iron Masters. He seems most at home in the city, which is a trait most Iron Masters bear. He hunts humans and sounds like Honor the Territory in all things is right in line for him. I tend to think of HtD as a bit more primal or feral. Stereotypes and all that. Especially a comic books guy.<br /> <br /> Plus the Technology gifts are Iron Master only and sound like they'd be really cool and useful for a superhero. He can Unmake criminal's guns, he can hijack their getaway vehicles with Iron Slave. He can stop an elevator or shut off their communication/calls for back up with Garble. He can use Shutdown to off the lights in a building to make a dramatic entrance.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as that makes sense, an Iron Master hunts humanity, not humans. Humanity exists even in the wilderness, you have oark rangers, hunters, survivalists, logging camps (i live in a forested area so its where my mind went). Just as any other tribe could also find themselves at home in a city as well. Spirits while not often active in high populous areas, they can be. Claimed usually go for humans, and I know spider hosts often take humans, and some Pure tribes are probably city based","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5448-kavagja","name":"Kavagja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T20:36:03-08:00","id":772040,"title":"","content":"Iron Masters are not the &quot;City&quot; Tribe. They are the &quot;Try Everything to find the best of anything&quot; Tribe. They are the &quot;Cutting Edge&quot; Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-23-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:23:25-08:00","id":772089,"title":"","content":"Iron Masters are city and only city is not a thing I said, but I'm sorry if I seemed to have implied that.<br /> <br /> Please forgive me, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:37:44-08:00","id":772097,"title":"","content":"*Just eagerly awaits for Urban gifts.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T02:32:01-08:00","id":772170,"title":"","content":"The Iron Masters are kind of the city tribe. They're not <i>exclusively </i>city, but if you asked &quot;who's the city tribe?&quot; Most people would say them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:34:56-08:00","id":772262,"title":"","content":"Simple - Iron Masters are <i><b>humanity</b></i> Tribe. Rest of the Tribes hunt for or against particular humans, Iron Masters hunts with or against humanity itself - they are Glasswalkers of <b>Forsaken</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other hand, Hunters in Darkness are Bone-Gnawers Tribe in the cities - they know the streets and territory better than no one. But they do not get <i>humans</i> living there. Iron Masters are for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}